.TH GOSSHD 8 "2026-11-06" "gosshd 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
gosshd \- Linux SSH server with a modern cryptographic baseline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gosshd
.RB [ \-4 | \-6 ]
.RB [ \-D ]
.RB [ \-e ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR config ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR time ]
.RB [ \-h
.IR host_key ]
.RB [ \-i ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR option ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-t ]
.RB [ \-T ]
.RB [ \-V ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gosshd
is a Linux SSH server built on the Go SSH implementation. It runs a
privileged monitor, an unprivileged worker per connection, and a session
launcher that drops to the target account. Forwarding is disabled.
.PP
Configuration is read from
.I /etc/ssh/sshd_config
by default. The parser supports includes, first-value-wins semantics, Match
blocks, a pre-authentication Banner, CASignatureAlgorithms enforcement,
full MaxStartups start:rate:full semantics, modern algorithm allowlists,
authorized commands, and explicit rejection of unsupported or weak
directives.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-4
Listen on IPv4 addresses only.
.TP
.B \-6
Listen on IPv6 addresses only.
.TP
.B \-D
Do not detach. Logs still go to syslog unless
.B \-e
is used.
.TP
.B \-e
Log to standard error instead of syslog.
.TP
.BI \-f " config"
Read configuration from
.IR config .
.TP
.BI \-g " time"
Override LoginGraceTime. A bare number is interpreted as seconds.
.TP
.BI \-h " host_key"
Add a host key file.
.TP
.B \-i
Run in inetd mode using standard input as the connection.
.TP
.BI \-o " option"
Apply a configuration option. May be repeated in the file but only one
command-line option is accepted.
.TP
.BI \-p " port"
Override the listening port.
.TP
.B \-t
Test the configuration and exit.
.TP
.B \-T
Print the effective configuration as JSON and exit. This is not the same
format as OpenSSH's
.BR sshd (8)
output.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload authentication and policy settings from the configuration file.
Changes to listeners, host keys, \fBPort\fR, \fBAddressFamily\fR,
\fBMaxStartups\fR, or \fBRequiredRSASize\fR require a restart.
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Stop accepting connections and shut down.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/sshd_config
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /etc/ssh/ssh_host_*_key
Default host key locations.
.TP
.I /etc/motd
Message of the day (when PrintMotd is enabled).
.TP
.I /var/log/lastlog
Last-login information (when PrintLastLog is enabled).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR sshd_config (5),
.BR ssh-keygen (1)
.SH NOTES
Forwarding, PAM, FIPS mode, and Ed448 are not supported in this build.
Authorized command output is treated as untrusted input.
.B UseDNS yes
is rejected because reverse-DNS host matching is not implemented; use
IP addresses or CIDR ranges in AllowUsers and DenyUsers. Compression values
other than
.B no
are rejected because the transport provides no compression. Banner is
available as a global directive only and is rejected inside Match.
Session processes are confined with Landlock: writes are allowed only under the user's home directory, /tmp, /var/tmp, /dev/shm, /dev, /proc, the session's runtime directory, and the configured chroot directory. The daemon refuses to start if the session sandbox is unavailable.
